;
; How Seedbank files one pin in MYRA (seedbank_rules.h SR5): its place in
; the pin table (0 .. 63), the block's size in bytes (at most 1048576),
; whether it was sealed at rest (1) or not (0), and when it was pinned, in
; seconds since 1970. Seedbank asks whether the numbers fit before it
; keeps them.
^ZXSEED(pin:i2) = bytes:i7! ^ sealed:i1! ^ stamp:i11!
